  "summary": "A roller chain drive transmits power positively (no slip) between sprockets. Rollers seat in the sprocket tooth gaps, so the speed ratio is exactly the tooth ratio (30/15 = 2:1). Chains handle high torque at low speed; they need lubrication and correct slack, provided here by a drip lubricator and an idler tensioner on the slack side.",
